-- title:
--   Dilatation of a quotient: surjectivity and π-saturated kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in R$, and let $C$ and $A$ be commutative rings (in the same universe as $R$) equipped with $R$-algebra structures, together with a $C$-algebra structure on $A$ making $R \to C \to A$ a scalar tower. Assume the structure map $C \to A$ is surjective, and let $J$ be an ideal of $C$. For an ideal $I$ of a commutative ring $B$ and an element $b \in B$, [`AffineDilatation.Ring I b`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20) denotes the $B$-subalgebra of the localization $B[1/b]$ generated by the set [`AffineDilatation.gen I b`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L13), that is, `Algebra.adjoin B (gen I b)`. The assertion is that there exists a $C$-algebra homomorphism $\theta'$ from [`AffineDilatation.Ring J (algebraMap R C π)`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20) to [`AffineDilatation.Ring (J.map (algebraMap C A)) (algebraMap R A π)`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20), where $J.map$ denotes the image ideal of $J$ in $A$, such that $\theta'$ is surjective and, for every $x$ in the source, $\theta' x = 0$ holds precisely when there is a natural number $\nu$ with $(\text{image of } \pi)^{\nu} \, x$ lying in the ideal of [`AffineDilatation.Ring J (algebraMap R C π)`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20) generated by the image of $\ker(C \to A)$ under the structure map of the dilatation. Only existence of such a $\theta'$ is claimed; no canonical choice or uniqueness is asserted.
--
--   This is the comparison of affine dilatations along a surjection, as in Bosch–Lütkebohmert–Raynaud's treatment of dilatations of schemes: the dilatation of a quotient is the quotient of the dilatation by the $\pi$-saturation of the extended kernel ideal. It feeds the affine step of the Néron-model smoothness bookkeeping, being cited by [`NeronModelInfra.smoothnessDefect_affineDilatation_add_one_le_of_isSmoothAt_of_mem_freeLocus`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.smoothnessDefect_affineDilatation_add_one_le_of_isSmoothAt_of_mem_freeLocus), where $C$ serves as a smooth ambient algebra presenting $A$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AffineDilatation_exists_algHom_surjective_ker_iff_of_surjective.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RingTheory_AffineDilatation

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

theorem AffineDilatation.exists_algHom_surjective_ker_iff_of_surjective
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (π : R)
    {C A : Type u} [CommRing C] [CommRing A] [Algebra R C] [Algebra R A] [Algebra C A] [IsScalarTower R C A]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap C A)) (J : Ideal C) :
    ∃ θ' : AffineDilatation.Ring J (algebraMap R C π) →ₐ[C]
        AffineDilatation.Ring (J.map (algebraMap C A)) (algebraMap R A π),
      Function.Surjective θ' ∧
      ∀ x : AffineDilatation.Ring J (algebraMap R C π),
        θ' x = 0 ↔ ∃ ν : ℕ, (algebraMap R _ π) ^ ν * x ∈
          (RingHom.ker (algebraMap C A)).map (algebraMap C (AffineDilatation.Ring J (algebraMap R C π))) := by sorry
